BT /F1 9 Tf 47 731.00 Td (WHY: The lecture describes a transient white reaction due to constriction; it is distinct from) Tj ET
BT /F1 9 Tf 47 717.50 Td (the classical red-flare-wheal response.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.4 Tf 47 702.00 Td (NOT A: Wheal is raised local oedema from permeability.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.4 Tf 47 688.40 Td (NOT B: The red line is a separate vasodilator response.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.4 Tf 47 674.80 Td (NOT C: Flare is surrounding redness from arteriolar dilation.) Tj ET
BT /F1 7 Tf 47 661.20 Td (SOURCE: lecture-6:Q49; 39-40) Tj ET
BT /F2 10 Tf 47 637.20 Td (31. D - Overlapping endothelial flaps admit interstitial fluid.) Tj ET
BT /F1 9 Tf 47 620.20 Td (WHY: Initial lymphatic endothelial flaps allow interstitial fluid and proteins to enter when) Tj ET
BT /F1 9 Tf 47 606.70 Td (surrounding pressure exceeds lymphatic pressure.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.4 Tf 47 591.20 Td (NOT A: Initial lymphatic capillaries lack a thick continuous smooth-muscle coat.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.4 Tf 47 577.60 Td (NOT B: There is no single central lymphatic heart.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.4 Tf 47 564.00 Td (NOT C: Initial lymphatics are relatively permeable to interstitial proteins.) Tj ET
BT /F1 7 Tf 47 550.40 Td (SOURCE: circulation-1:Q93; 60; Chapter 15 2) Tj ET
BT /F2 10 Tf 47 526.40 Td (32. D - Other conducting tissues retain latent automaticity.) Tj ET
BT /F1 9 Tf 47 509.40 Td (WHY: Subsidiary pacemakers in the AV junction or Purkinje system can spontaneously depolarise,) Tj ET
BT /F1 9 Tf 47 495.90 Td (usually at slower rates.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.4 Tf 47 480.40 Td (NOT A: Autonomic nerves modify pacemaking but do not directly activate every myocyte.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.4 Tf 47 466.80 Td (NOT B: Coordinated contraction still requires electrical activation.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.4 Tf 47 453.20 Td (NOT C: Valves are passive mechanical structures.) Tj ET
BT /F1 7 Tf 47 439.60 Td (SOURCE: circulation-1:Q13; 7; Chapter 3 4) Tj ET
BT /F2 10 Tf 47 415.60 Td (33. C - The arterial baroreflex reacts to the sympathetic pressure rise.) Tj ET
BT /F1 9 Tf 47 398.60 Td (WHY: Medullary ischaemia first raises sympathetic pressure; arterial baroreceptors then increase) Tj ET
BT /F1 9 Tf 47 385.10 Td (vagal drive and slow the heart.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.4 Tf 47 369.60 Td (NOT A: beta1 stimulation would usually accelerate, not slow, the heart.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.4 Tf 47 356.00 Td (NOT B: Cardiac autonomic signalling remains central to the response.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.4 Tf 47 342.40 Td (NOT D: Atrial volume receptors respond chiefly to filling, not this sequence.) Tj ET
