BT /F2 10 Tf 47 304.80 Td (34. C - Hypoxia together with accumulating carbon dioxide.) Tj ET
BT /F1 9 Tf 47 287.80 Td (WHY: Poor medullary perfusion produces hypoxia and hypercapnia, which strongly stimulate the) Tj ET
BT /F1 9 Tf 47 274.30 Td (vasomotor centre to raise pressure.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.4 Tf 47 258.80 Td (NOT A: High oxygen and low CO2 do not represent medullary ischaemia.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.4 Tf 47 245.20 Td (NOT B: Low acidity and abundant oxygen oppose the described stimulus.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.4 Tf 47 231.60 Td (NOT D: Adequate oxygen delivery would not produce the ischaemic response.) Tj ET
